Lokalizacja: Polska

O nas:&nbsp;

RTB House to globalna firma dostarczająca najnowocześniejsze technologie marketingowe dla największych marek i agencji na całym świecie. Autorski mechanizm zakupu reklam jest pierwszym na świecie opartym w całości o algorytmy Deep Learning. Umożliwia reklamodawcom osiągać wyjątkowe efekty i realizować cele na każdym etapie lejka sprzedażowego.

Założoną w 2012 firmę&nbsp; RTB House tworzy ponad 1000 specjalistów w przeszło 30 lokalizacjach na całym świecie. RTB House obsługuje ponad 3000 kampanii dla klientów z regionów EMEA, APAC i obu Ameryk.

Twoje zadania:&nbsp;

• Kompleksowa obsługa systemu do elektronicznego obiegu dokumentów księgowych, w tym ich weryfikacja i nadzorowanie obiegu;

• Rozliczanie zaliczek i kart służbowych;

• Rozliczanie podróży i wydatków służbowych;

• Wsparcie w zakresie obsługi płatności;

• Wsparcie w przygotowywaniu raportów finansowych na potrzeby wewnętrzne i zarządcze.

Wymagane doświadczenie:&nbsp;

• 1-3 lata doświadczenia w pracy na podobnym stanowisku (mile widziane doświadczenie w biurze rachunkowym);

• Praktyczna znajomość zagadnień księgowo-podatkowych;

• Praktyczna znajomość obsługi programu MS Excel oraz Google Sheets;

• Mile widziane doświadczenie w pracy z narzędziami AI;

• Język angielski na poziomie min. B2;

• Wykształcenie wyższe (preferowany kierunek: finanse i rachunkowość);

• Samodzielność i dobra organizacja własnej pracy;

• Zdolności analityczne i dokładność;

• Odpowiedzialność oraz umiejętność współpracy w zespole.

Oferujemy:&nbsp;

• Współpracę w dynamicznie rozwijającej się międzynarodowej organizacji, dążącej do pozycji lidera w Europe i na świecie.

• Długofalową współpracę w oparciu o umowę zlecenie lub B2B.&nbsp;

• Elastyczne formy współpracy - zdalna lub hybrydowa (biuro przy metrze Wilanowska).

• Przyjazną atmosferę współpracy z zorganizowanym gronem profesjonalistów i w poszanowaniu zasad work-life balance.

&nbsp;

Aplikuj już teraz!&nbsp;

Aby aplikować, nie musisz spełniać wszystkich wymagań. Jeżeli interesuje Cię rozwój w obszarze kadr, prześlij do nas swoje CV, a my je sprawdzimy.

At NiCE, we don’t limit our challenges. We challenge our limits. Always. We’re ambitious. We’re game changers. And we play to win. We set the highest standards and execute beyond them. And if you’re like us, we can offer you the ultimate career opportunity that will light a fire within you.

So, what’s the role all about? &nbsp;

NiCE is looking for a Senior Product Manager to lead the definition and hands ‑ on creation of the NiCE Agentic Engagement Plane (AEP)..&nbsp; NiCE’s AEP is the next-generation architecture for the contact center. It is the coordination layer above channels, AI providers, and the human workforce where every customer engagement becomes the durable unit of work, and existing CRM and CDP systems persist as memory rather than getting ripped out.&nbsp; &nbsp;

In this role, you will own innovative capabilities across the NiCE AEP, shaping how AI understands customer interactions, for effective system and/or agent handoff. You will have the opportunity to personally design, prototype, and validate AI ‑ driven product experiences.  &nbsp;

You will be responsible for building the next generation of AI ‑ powered CX solutions-not just features, but intelligent systems and working prototypes-while maintaining NiCE’s standards for security, governance, and enterprise readiness. &nbsp;

This is a highly hands ‑ on product role, ideal for a Product Manager who enjoys building, experimenting, and turning ideas into tangible product artifacts quickly. &nbsp;

  &nbsp;

How will you make an impact?    &nbsp;

• Identifying real market and customer problems through research, data analysis, and direct customer engagement-and rapidly turning insights into working product prototypes &nbsp;

• Driving AI ‑ first product strategy, ensuring that AI is designed as a foundation for outcomes, not just an add ‑ on feature &nbsp;

• Using prototypes as a core decision ‑ making tool-to explore solutions, de ‑ risk complexity, and accelerate time ‑ to ‑ value &nbsp;

• Delivering clear, actionable roadmaps and strategic plans that are grounded in validated product concepts, not assumptions &nbsp;

• Championing customer experience excellence through experimentation, iteration, and feedback ‑ driven improvements &nbsp;

• Collaborating in a truly cross ‑ functional environment, where product, engineering, and data teams work as one &nbsp;

• Leading data ‑ driven decision making, using analytics, experimentation, and model performance insights to guide priorities and trade ‑ offs &nbsp;

• Helping NiCE stay ahead of the market by bringing innovation, speed, and hands ‑ on AI fluency into everything we build &nbsp;

If you’re excited about building AI products-not just defining them, and want to shape the future of CX with real impact, this is the role for you. &nbsp;

  &nbsp;

Have you got what it takes? &nbsp;

• 5+ years of software product management experience, delivering enterprise ‑ grade cloud solutions &nbsp;

• Own the roadmap set direction, prioritize, and keep it current &nbsp;

• Own domain expertise for your service area: AI capabilities, competitive landscape, customer adoption, and real-world production performance &nbsp;

• Proven hands ‑ on experience working on AI ‑ powered, data ‑ driven, or automation ‑ centric products &nbsp;

• Strong technical understanding, with the ability to personally prototype solutions and work deeply with engineering and data science teams &nbsp;

• Experience influencing decisions across multiple global stakeholders and functions &nbsp;

• Strong analytical and problem ‑ solving skills, with a bias toward outcomes and execution &nbsp;

• Experience translating concepts and ideas into concrete product artifacts (prototypes, flows, experiments, validation plans) &nbsp;

• Excellent communication skills-able to engage effectively from executive leadership to individual contributors &nbsp;

• Ability to manage multiple initiatives in parallel and thrive in a fast ‑ paced environment &nbs

Volunteer Program at PE Insights

Germany's Largest PE Conference. Frankfurt, March 15th &amp; 16th 2027

&nbsp;

Ready to take a major leap towards private equity, M&amp;A, banking or consulting? This is your chance to get a view behind the scenes of the world’s largest private equity community and be part of the volunteer team shaping the future of finance.

Challenge yourself to go outside your comfort zone with likeminded individuals who for two days will be your partners in the trenches facilitating the room of top-of-the pyramid PE professionals.

&nbsp;

Why Private Equity Insights

Private Equity Insights is the world’s largest Private Equity community with 1m PE professionals, delivering impact through 12 global PE conferences with thousands of the most world’s best investors and operators such as Blackstone, BlackRock, Apollo, Carlyle, CVC, KKR, and many more.&nbsp;

Private Equity Insights is part of United Media (https://www.united-media.com/) which focuses on building large-scale industry media and conferences products in sectors such as insurance, finance, retail, etc. As of today, we have organically launched 5 media companies and exited 1.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

What we offer you

You’ll be supporting the Private Equity Insights team in delivering the conference for sharp insights and inspiration, and outstanding network opportunities for the PE professionals we serve. Among other things the opportunity offer:

• Peer network: you join a select group of ambitious volunteers who will keep crossing your path for the next 40 years working in the industry.

• Insider knowledge. Where the day allows, you can sit in on panels, the same ones attendees come to hear. In fact, we encourage you to do so.

• Confidence under pressure: after two demanding conference days, high-stakes moments at work will feel easier.

• Master persuasion: learn to influence high-caliber professionals to deliver win-win results.&nbsp;

• A certificate to show on your CV and LinkedIn that you volunteered at Private Equity Insights.&nbsp;

• Fuel: food and refreshments on both days.

• Global programme: The long term opportunity to lead teams and become the person who shows the way for others, or even join Private Equity Insights full time.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Your responsibilities

This is hands-on, operational work focusing on making the conference run. The work changes hour by hour, and you are expected to step in and help wherever the conference needs you.

&nbsp;

What the future hold for you with PE Insights&nbsp;

Whether you are with us for 1 conference or 10+, we believe this lays the foundation for a very successful career.&nbsp;

Exceptional volunteers have in the past been offered roles at Private Equity Insights, such as Investor Relations or Entrepreneur in Residence.

Others have gone on to join firms such as McKinsey, BCG, JP Morgan, Deutsche Bank, Ardian and Verdane.

&nbsp;

What we expect from you

We are looking for final-year undergraduates, master's students and early-career professionals with an interest in private equity, M&amp;A, banking, consulting or conferences. We expect you to:

• Have a relentless drive to become the very best at what you do

• Bring outstanding energy and a positive mindset from the first hour to the last

• Set aside 2 full days for the conference + online training leading up to

• Be curious to learn from top private equity professionals

• Stand out as the person others want beside them on a hard day

• Speak English at a professional level. Spanish is a plus

&nbsp;

This is an unpaid role. Applicants from outside Frankfurt are welcome. You fully arrange your own travel and accommodation.&nbsp;

We review every application and invite shortlisted candidates to a short call. If you hold yourself to the standard described here, apply.

